  "rationale": {
    "CVE-2026-107496": "The vulnerable CMS_encrypt/CMS_encrypt_ex path with an untrusted EC recipient certificate is not called. The only externally supplied device key is canonical P-256 SPKI used for ECDSA verification; the reviewed source does not accept CMS recipients, invoke CMS encryption or expose arbitrary crypto/subprocess selection. The cryptography bundled OpenSSL 4.0.1 copy also lacks enable-ec_explicit_curves; this additional mitigation is not assumed for the system or libpq copies.",
    "CVE-2026-88823": "The vulnerable AES-GCM-SIV decryption implementation is not called: the exact reviewed ERP source uses AESGCM only. This assessment includes all three image-bound OpenSSL copies and is invalidated by any source, dependency, native inventory, configuration/provider or startup change.",
    "CVE-2026-95691": "The QUIC client path is unreachable. Pinned CPython _ssl uses TLS_method/TLS_client_method/TLS_server_method; pinned libpq 18 uses SSLv23_method. The exact reviewed ERP uses ordinary TLS clients, not OSSL_QUIC_client_method or arbitrary transport selection. Complete ELF, application, startup and provider/configuration closure is required.",
    "CVE-2026-95692": "The image-bound application and startup source use AESGCM with a 12-byte nonce, never AES-GCM-SIV or caller-selected cipher APIs. Complete native closure covers system OpenSSL 3.5.9, psycopg-binary private libraries, and cryptography 50.0.0 bundled OpenSSL 4.0.1. The vulnerable AES-GCM-SIV initialization path is not called. Scope requires unchanged source, lock, native bytes, startup, provider/configuration and deployment environment."
  },
